      "noteControls": {
        "definitionVersion": 1,
        "id": "noteControls",
        "label": "notecontrols1",
        "parameters": {
          "body": "A widget is a value node: no picture, one number you set by hand, read as op('heat').chan.heat.\nHeat is brightness and Invert flips it. Next hue turns the hue a quarter. Top-right pin drags the picture's corner.\nDrag it on its node or on the Panel. Button adds flashCount; XY Pad publishes warpX and warpY.",
          "color": "input",
          "title": "Controls"
        },
        "position": {
          "x": -1500,
          "y": 800
        },
        "size": {
          "height": 200,
          "width": 1078
        },
        "type": "annotate"
      },
      "noteMapping": {
        "definitionVersion": 1,
        "id": "noteMapping",
        "label": "notemapping1",
        "parameters": {
          "body": "Right-click a parameter in the Inspector → Control from Panel: it makes the control, binds it and adds it to the Panel.\nDrive from ▸ binds a control you already have. A bound parameter shows ← Heat.\nUnderneath is an expression: op('heat').chan.heat. It is maths: op('flash').chan.flashCount * 90 turns the hue a quarter per press.",
          "color": "value",
          "title": "Mapping: a parameter follows a control"
        },
        "position": {
          "x": -1500,
          "y": -300
        },
        "size": {
          "height": 240,
          "width": 740
        },
        "type": "annotate"
      },
      "notePanel": {
        "definitionVersion": 1,
        "id": "notePanel",
        "label": "notepanel1",
        "parameters": {
          "body": "A widget joins panel1 by a wire: its out into the Panel's Controls, or drop the widget on the Panel.\nThe Panel is a board: the pencil in the Controls tab moves and sizes each control and adds labels.\nIts body on the canvas is the same board, live. The Controls tab is a bigger view of it.\nThe phone icon on its header publishes it to a paired phone.",
          "color": "composite",
          "title": "Panel"
        },
        "position": {
          "x": 240,
          "y": 260
        },
        "size": {
          "height": 260,
          "width": 520
        },
        "type": "annotate"
      },
      "notePhone": {
        "definitionVersion": 1,
        "id": "notePhone",
        "label": "notephone1",
        "parameters": {
          "body": "1. Start the helper: pnpm helper --phone\n2. Pair it in Agent → Connections.\n3. Press the phone icon on panel1's header and scan the QR code.\n4. Accept the certificate once. The phone shows this panel and nothing else.\nA phone can also be a camera: in a Webcam node pick the device Phone · <name>.",
          "color": "color",
          "title": "Phone"
        },
        "position": {
          "x": 240,
          "y": 560
        },
        "size": {
          "height": 260,
          "width": 520
        },
        "type": "annotate"
      },
      "noteSurface": {
        "definitionVersion": 1,
        "id": "noteSurface",
        "label": "notesurface1",
        "parameters": {
          "body": "pin1 pins the picture's four corners onto the output.\nDrag the pins on its preview tile to fit a wall.\nThe top-right pin reads the pad: pintr x is op('warp').chan.warpX, y is op('warp').chan.warpY.",
          "color": "output",
          "title": "Mapping to a surface: Corner Pin"
